    "turn_text": "Welcome to She Thinks a podcast where you're allowed to think for yourself. I'm your host Beverly Hallberg, and on today's episode, Congresswoman Kat Kamik joins us to talk about the increasing crisis on our southern border, what the defund the police movement has meant to communities across the country, and finally, what does it look like to stand up for law enforcement in today's climate? But before we bring her on a little bit more about the Congresswoman, Representative Kat Kamik proudly serves Florida's third congressional district as the youngest Republican woman and the 117th Congress. She is a third-generation sandblaster who grew up on a cattle ranch and understands the hard work and determination it takes to run a small business. A proud alumnus of the Naval War College cat knows the issues and constituents of Florida's third intimately having served as the longtime former deputy chief of staff for the district prior to her election in 2020 Congresswoman. Thank you so much for joining she thinks today. Hey, thanks for having me glad to be here. So first question for you is what is it like to be the youngest Republican woman in Congress?",
